 2 7.6M3.6 8.4V14h3.2v-3.2h2.4V14h3.2V8.4"></path></svg></a><span>/</span><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white rounded-sm" href="/docs/community/community-intro">Community</a><span>/</span><a class="transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-black dark:hover:text-white rounded-sm" href="/guides">Guides</a></div><article><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-6 sm:flex-col sm:items-stretch sm:gap-4"><div class="max-w-xl 2xl:max-w-[520px]"><h1 class="text-[36px] leading-tight font-medium tracking-tighter text-balance md:text-[28px]">Building a Job Queue System with Node.js, Bull, and Neon Postgres</h1><p class="mt-[1.125rem] text-xl leading-tight tracking-extra-tight text-gray-new-40 dark:text-gray-new-70 md:mt-1.5 md:text-lg">Learn how to implement a job queue system to handle background tasks efficiently using Node.js, Bull, and Neon Postgres</p></div><div class="relative mt-2.5 w-fit sm:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center border border-gray-new-90 dark:border-gray-new-20"><button class="flex h-8 w-fit shrink-0 items-center gap-2 border-r border-gray-new-90 px-2.5 whitespace-nowrap text-black-new hover:bg-gray-new-98 dark:border-gray-new-20 dark:text-gray-new-94 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="size-4 shrink-0"><g clip-path="url(#copy-docs_inline_svg__a)"><mask id="copy-docs_inline_svg__b" width="16" height="16" x="0" y="0" maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" style="mask-type:luminance"><path fill="#fff" d="M0 0h16v16H0z"></path></mask><g stroke="currentColor" mask="url(#copy-docs_inline_svg__b)"><path d="M5.947 14.63h8.683V5.945H5.947z"></path><path d="M3.579 10.684H2V2h8.683v1.579"></path></g></g><defs><clipPath id="copy-docs_inline_svg__a"><path fill="#fff" d="M0 0h16v16H0z"></path></clipPath></defs></svg><span class="text-sm leading-none tracking-extra-tight whitespace-nowrap">Copy page</span></button><button class="flex h-8 items-center px-1 hover:bg-gray-new-98 dark:hover:bg-gray-new-8"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="15" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 15" class="size-3.5 text-gray-new-50 transition-transform duration-200 dark:text-gray-new-50"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" d="M3.5 5.75 7 9.25l3.5-3.5"></path></svg></button></div></div></div><div class="prose-doc post-content prose dark:prose-invert xs:prose-code:break-words mt-10 lg:mt-7 md:mt-5"><p>Job queues are essential components in modern applications. Queues enable you to handle resource-intensive or time-consuming tasks asynchronously. This approach improves application responsiveness by moving heavy processing out of the request-response cycle.</p>
<p>In this guide, we&#x27;ll walk through building a job queue system using Node.js, Bull (a Redis-backed queue library), and Neon Postgres to process jobs efficiently at scale.</p>
<h2 id="prerequisites" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Prerequisites</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#prerequisites" aria-label="Link to Prerequisites"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>To follow the steps in this guide, you will need the following:</p>
<ul>
<li><a class="group inline" href="https://nodejs.org/en" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Node.js 18<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> or later</li>
<li>A <a class="group inline" href="https://console.neon.tech/signup" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neon<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> account</li>
<li><a class="group inline" href="https://redis.io/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Redis<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> installed locally</li>
<li>Basic understanding of JavaScript and PostgreSQL</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="understanding-job-queues" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Understanding Job Queues</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#understanding-job-queues" aria-label="Link to Understanding Job Queues"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>Job queues allow applications to offload time-consuming tasks to be processed in the background. Some common use cases include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Email delivery</li>
<li>Image or video processing</li>
<li>Data aggregation and reporting</li>
<li>Webhook delivery</li>
<li>Regular maintenance tasks</li>
</ul>
<p>Here&#x27;s how our architecture will work:</p>
<ol>
<li>The main application adds jobs to the queue</li>
<li>Bull manages the queue in Redis</li>
<li>Worker processes consume jobs from the queue</li>
<li>Job statuses and results are stored in Neon Postgres</li>
<li>The application can check job status and retrieve results</li>
</ol>
<p>This separation improves system performance, reliability, and scalability. It also allows for better error handling, retry logic, monitoring and even user experience as the application can respond quickly to user requests regardless of the job processing time.</p>
<h2 id="create-a-neon-project" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Create a Neon project</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#create-a-neon-project" aria-label="Link to Create a Neon project"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>First, let&#x27;s set up a new Neon Postgres database to store our job metadata.</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p>Navigate to the <a class="group inline" href="https://console.neon.tech/app/projects" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neon Console<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> and create a new project.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Choose a name for your project, for example &quot;job-queue-system&quot;.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>After creating the project, you&#x27;ll see the connection details. Save the connection string, you&#x27;ll need it to connect to your database.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Using the SQL Editor in the Neon Console or your preferred PostgreSQL client, create the tables for our job queue system:</p>
</li>
</ol>
